      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe this is okay for landing this CL and making progress, but IIUC here we are pinky-promising to the compiler that we got the function signature correct, and that the `.h` file didn\u0027t change some time after we copied the signature.  So I think we should try to avoid this in the long term.  If this is hard to resolve, then can you please add a TODO comment about this?\n\nI am not sure how exactly to avoid this though... let me share some initial, unbaked ideas:\n\n* Would it be possible to use `#[cxx::bridge]` as done for the other things?  Or would that lead to an explicit circular dependency in the build graph?  Implicit circular dependencies are probably also somewhat undesirable although this one seems ok to me for the short term...\n* Alternatively, maybe `#[cxx::bridge]` could support things better with a slightly redesigned API?  A few alternatives to consider:\n    - A function pointer to `skcms_ApproximateCurve` can be theoretically passed as an argument to `parse_icc_profile`?\n    - Or maybe Rust can return a Rust-only data structures and then C/C++ side can drive finishing the conversion (e.g. calling `skcms_ApproximateCurve`)?",
